	"data": "Networking Hardware & Fundamentals\n\nA learning track for understanding the physical and logical infrastructure that connects devices — switches, routers, VLANs, PoE, subnetting, and beyond.\n\nWhy This Matters\n\nThe homelab runs on networking. Every device — Pi 5, Optiplex, Star, Quest 3, Shelly relays, Satellite1, ESP32 nodes — talks through the network. Right now the knowledge is patchy: I know what a switch does at a surface level, but not the differences between managed and unmanaged, how…",
